  R"LPROFILE({"schema":"loom.runtime_profile/1","domain":"intent_routing","revision":1,"description":"Everything from the conversation window (R54, GRAF_HUB_KOD_SILNIK §8): every chat input goes through input.route_intent, which decides message or command and, for a command, resolves it against the action catalogue and the rules and answers IN the conversation with a proposal. This profile is the data of that decision. method: heuristic (local and free: explicit command syntax, patterns, and the phrases that actions carry in the catalogue; no model call; the preset), model (one use_model call with the configured model, guarded like every other), hybrid (the local reading first, the model only for what it is unsure of; recommended once a provider key exists), off (every input is a message). The method is a setting: config key `intent_routing_method`, then the preset below; the call may override it. execution: whether a proposal waits for the user's yes (propose, the preset), runs at once when the whole plan only reads and the rules ask for nothing (read_only), or runs at once whatever it does (always); the rules and the x10 usage confirmation apply in every case. Confirmation is a reply that is exactly one of the yes / no words below. A phrase on an action is space-separated words, all of which must occur within `window_tokens` of the start with at least one within `lead_tokens`; a word ending in * matches any continuation; text is lower-cased and the letters in `fold` are replaced before matching. A chat input is a command only when it names an action AND an element (an id, or a word that refers to the conversation or a message); otherwise it is a message and continues on the chat path unchanged. All numbers here are calibration, not limits: the user's overlay <data>/profiles/intent_routing.pack changes any of them.","defaults":{"method":{"setting":"intent_routing_method","active":"heuristic","presets":{"off":{"label":{"en":"Off: every input is a message","pl":"Wyłą